  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who grew up in households where corporal punishment was used as a form of discipline, or who have a nostalgic or humorous appreciation for historical parenting practices. The meme appeals to those who can relate to the experience of being disciplined for talking back, using the visual of a historical scene to evoke shared memories or humor. The audience is likely to include adults who recall or have heard stories about strict, traditional parenting from the past, and who may view the image as a lighthearted or ironic commentary on childhood discipline. The meme's intent to normalize or romanticize corporal punishment may resonate with those who have a personal connection to such practices, even if it is considered harmful by modern child welfare norms.",
